{"query": {"id": "20260628162109677541_a1bfc805", "handle": "q2", "text": 
"\"Ring of Nestor\" archaeological object discovery context", "importance": 
"core"}, "items": [{"id": "20260628162225864029_f9e8ab89", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The Heidelberg University Library access page describes Arthur J. 
Evans' monograph \"The ring of Nestor\" (1925) as consisting of two main 
sections: (I) \"Sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia\" (pp. 1–42), and (II) \"A glimpse into the Minoan after-world\"
(pp. 43–75), followed by plates I–V, and states that the work analyses a group 
of gold signet rings and bead seals found at Thisbê in Boeotia, interpreted as a
sepulchral treasure associated with Minoan iconography and beliefs.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628162224666520_47a6ceb5"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628162225943566_60534243", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The access-page 
summary notes that within the first section Evans describes \"the circumstances 
of the discovery of the treasure at Thisbê, including its location in Boeotia, 
the nature of the burial context, and the association of the material with a 
tomb,\" and that he \"details the archaeologists and local authorities involved 
in bringing the treasure to scholarly attention.\"", "source_ids": 
["20260628162224666520_47a6ceb5"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628162226022279_4497e581", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Heidelberg 
description specifies that Evans' work provides \"measurements, descriptions, 
and iconographic analyses of the individual rings,\" and identifies among these 
objects \"the so-called 'Ring of Nestor'\" as featuring prominently.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628162224666520_47a6ceb5"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628162226103805_3e816b59", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Heidelberg 
page indicates that Evans situates the rings within broader \"Minoan and 
Mycenaean cultural contexts,\" discusses \"stylistic dating,\" and compares them
\"with other Aegean signet rings,\" framing the second section as \"a 'glimpse 
into the Minoan after-world'.\"", "source_ids": 
["20260628162224666520_47a6ceb5"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628162226184548_22335f07", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Heidelberg 
scroll-view interface lists the table of contents for Evans' work, including the
headings \"I. Sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia\" and \"II. A glimpse into the Minoan after-world\" and notes 
the presence of plates I–V.", "source_ids": ["20260628162224696610_c9b6bb83"], 
"citations": [7]}, {"id": "20260628162226264054_31dca868", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The HathiTrust catalog record identifies the work \"ʻThe ring of 
Nestor;̓ a glimpse into the Minoan after-world, and a sepulchral treasure of gold
signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia\" with author \"Evans, Arthur 
J. (Arthur John), 1851–1941\" and publication information \"London, 1925.\"", 
"source_ids": ["20260628162224726379_c2ff62df"], "citations": [8]}, {"id": 
"20260628162226342689_f2703527", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The HathiTrust 
description states that Evans' work concerns \"a sepulchral treasure of gold 
signet rings and bead seals from Thisbê, Boeotia,\" and presents it in 
connection with \"the Minoan after-world,\" thereby linking the Ring of Nestor 
to a funerary assemblage from Thisbê.", "source_ids": 
["20260628162224726379_c2ff62df"], "citations": [8]}, {"id": 
"20260628162226419683_1b6fbfed", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Academia.edu 
abstract for \"SOME OBSERVATIONS ON THE ICONOGRAPHY OF THE ‘RING OF NESTOR’\" 
indicates that the paper offers an analysis of the Ring of Nestor's iconography 
in the \"context of Aegean forgeries and authenticity debates\" and that it 
revisits key features of the imagery and comparative material to assess the 
ring's significance in Minoan and Mycenaean art.", "source_ids": 
["20260628162220158891_7c0d11cf"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628162226500789_69be1d2b", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The snippet from 
the article mentions that the connection between \"incurved altars\" and the 
depiction on the Ring of Nestor is used to support the ring's authenticity, and 
notes that the authenticity of both \"Nestor's and Minos' rings\" has been 
subject to debate among scholars.", "source_ids": 
["20260628162220158891_7c0d11cf"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628162439693011_a07e8cfc", "type": "Claim", "text": "Arthur J. Evans’s 
1925 monograph \"The ring of Nestor\" examines a sepulchral treasure of gold 
signet rings and bead seals discovered at Thisbê in Boeotia, Greece, among which
the so‑called Ring of Nestor is a principal object.", "source_ids": 
["20260628162224666520_47a6ceb5", "20260628162224696610_c9b6bb83", 
"20260628162224726379_c2ff62df"], "citations": [6, 7, 8]}, {"id": 
"20260628162440104444_ce43be95", "type": "Claim", "text": "Evans describes the 
discovery circumstances of the Thisbê sepulchral treasure—its location in 
Boeotia, its association with a tomb and burial context, and the involvement of 
archaeologists and local authorities in bringing the finds, including the Ring 
of Nestor, to scholarly attention.", "source_ids": 
["20260628162224666520_47a6ceb5"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628162440208284_1839f799", "type": "Claim", "text": "Evans interprets the 
Ring of Nestor and related rings from the Thisbê treasure as evidence for 
Minoan‑related beliefs about the afterlife, presenting them within a broader 
discussion of a \"Minoan after‑world\" and situating their style in Minoan and 
Mycenaean cultural contexts.", "source_ids": ["20260628162224666520_47a6ceb5", 
"20260628162224726379_c2ff62df"], "citations": [6, 8]}, {"id": 
"20260628162440382424_e92a12d8", "type": "Claim", "text": "Modern scholarship 
has repeatedly questioned the authenticity of the Ring of Nestor, debating 
whether it is a genuine Aegean antiquity or a later forgery, and some arguments 
in favor of its authenticity refer to iconographic features such as incurved 
altars.", "source_ids": ["20260628162220158891_7c0d11cf"], "citations": [3]}], 
"offset": 0, "limit": 50, "total": 13, "next_offset": null}
[tools:e2c35e3f-da02-190a-a428-993a7b566140] [get_report_evidence result] 
{"query": {"id": "20260628162109832593_8eb5f456", "handle": "q3", "text": 
"\"Ring of Nestor\" catalogue entry PDF", "importance": "supporting"}, "items": 
[{"id": "20260628162221997021_1c9b03fb", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"论文将“Ring of 
Nestor”定义为一枚金质印章戒指，表面刻有树及守护者等图像，属于爱琴海晚期青铜时代
艺术讨论范围。", "source_ids": ["20260628162220085816_fdec2493"], "citations": 
[1]}, {"id": "20260628162222073264_47605726", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"Vlachopoulos 引述 Evans 
对戒指守护者形象的描述，称其为“watch-dog”或“dragon”，并将场景理解为涉及一棵象征
性的“tree of the world”。", "source_ids": ["20260628162220085816_fdec2493"], 
"citations": [1]}, {"id": "20260628162222150433_9451c746", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "文章回顾了将“Ring of 
Nestor”视为晚期青铜时代爱琴海艺术作品的传统观点与将其视作近代伪作的反对意见，构
成关于该戒指真实性的系统学术综述。", "source_ids": 
["20260628162220085816_fdec2493"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628162222235342_3afd4745", "type": "Evidence", "text": "论文将“Ring of 
Nestor”纳入爱琴海宗教与葬俗图像学研究，讨论其图像可能关联来世观念、树崇拜及守护
者形象的意义。", "source_ids": ["20260628162220085816_fdec2493"], "citations": 
[1]}, {"id": "20260628162222325838_85314c42", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"《Journal of Hellenic Studies》论文将“Ring of Nestor”归入 Thisbê 
墓葬中发现的金质印章戒指和珠形封印宝藏，并以此作为讨论米诺斯来世观念的核心文物之
一。", "source_ids": ["20260628162220119862_244c3281"], "citations": [2]}, 
{"id": "20260628162222407679_d75caadb", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"该期刊文章从图像学角度解读戒指上的树、人物和守护者场景，认为它们构成对“米诺斯来
世世界”的象征性呈现，可能涉及宗教仪式和死者在来世的状态。", "source_ids": 
["20260628162220119862_244c3281"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628162222481706_cf2a1d33", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"期刊论文据称提供“Ring of 
Nestor”的材质、尺寸和年代归属说明，将其视作金质印章戒指，年代约为晚期米诺斯或迈
锡尼时期。", "source_ids": ["20260628162220119862_244c3281"], "citations": [2]},
{"id": "20260628162222570298_6ad7b371", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“Some 
observations on the iconography of the ‘Ring of 
Nestor’”一文对戒指图像中的树、动物和人物等元素进行细致观察，讨论其布局和图像含义
，并检验这些特征是否与已知米诺斯及迈锡尼文物图像相似。", "source_ids": 
["20260628162220158891_7c0d11cf"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628162222655991_817d0dae", "type": "Evidence", "text": "论文将“Ring of 
Nestor”放入爱琴海伪作或可疑文物的讨论之中，通过比较其图像元素与既有文物资料来评
估其真实性。", "source_ids": ["20260628162220158891_7c0d11cf"], "citations": 
[3]}, {"id": "20260628162222742155_5e16bd98", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"作者引用并评述 Karo 和 Evans 等学者此前对“Ring of 
Nestor”的看法，以展示真品与伪作两种立场在图像学分析中的依据。", "source_ids": 
